Gears of War 3: native surfaces keep depth to colour EDRAM ownership copies. Gears 3 reads its
scene depth back through colour surfaces at the same EDRAM base; with those copies dropped,
character lighting in cutscenes went dark (found with gpu_native_surfaces_keep, 0081). No
measurable frame rate cost at 2x.

diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/pipeline/render_target/native_surfaces.h b/include/rex/graphics/pipeline/render_target/native_surfaces.h
index a467911..47b3592 100644
--- a/include/rex/graphics/pipeline/render_target/native_surfaces.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/pipeline/render_target/native_surfaces.h
@@ -53,9 +53,12 @@ inline bool KeepListMatches(const std::string& list, const SurfaceKind& source,
   return false;
 }
 
+// Gears of War 3 recomp: and depth to colour. Gears 3 reads its scene depth back through colour
+// surfaces at the same EDRAM base (D0x1 to C0x1 / C2x1 / C3x1 / C5x1 / C6x1); dropped, character
+// lighting in cutscenes went dark. Keeping them cost no measurable frame rate at 2x.
 inline bool KeepTransfer(const SurfaceKind& source, const SurfaceKind& dest) {
   if (!dest.is_depth) {
-    return false;
+    return source.is_depth;
   }
   return source.is_depth || source.format == kColorFormat16_16;
 }
